        Farms are the harshest service environment wire mesh faces: constant moisture, manure chemistry, soil contact, animal impact, and UV exposure—often all at once. A mesh that survives ten years on a factory wall can fail in eighteen months on a pasture fence line. Choosing correctly at purchase time is far cheaper than replacing a 2 km perimeter fence twice.
      </p>
